{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block content %}
{% set latest = years[-1] %}
<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">Every year the American Society of Human Genetics picks a few hundred of its several thousand accepted
abstracts for a talk; the rest become posters. This site parses the published abstract booklets
({{ years[0].year }}–{{ latest.year }}) and asks which phrases, institutions and places show up more often among talks.</p>
<p class="caveat"><strong>Read this first.</strong> The booklets list only <em>accepted</em> abstracts, and authors
can ask for a poster. "Talk rate" is the fraction of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, not an acceptance
rate or a quality score. Every number here is an association.</p>

<div class="stats">
{% for y in years %}
  <a class="stat" href="phrases.html#{{ y.year }}">
    <div class="where">ASHG {{ y.year }}{% if y.host %} · {{ y.host }}{% endif %}</div>
    <div class="big">{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * y.summary.talk_rate) }}%</div>
    <div class="small">talk rate: {{ "{:,}".format(y.summary.talks) }} talks of {{ "{:,}".format(y.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts</div>
  </a>
{% endfor %}
{% if pooled %}
  <a class="stat" href="#all-years">
    <div class="where">All years · {{ pooled.label }}</div>
    <div class="big">{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * pooled.summary.talk_rate) }}%</div>
    <div class="small">talk rate: {{ "{:,}".format(pooled.summary.talks) }} talks of {{ "{:,}".format(pooled.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts</div>
  </a>
{% endif %}
</div>

{% if pooled %}
{% set p = pooled %}
<h2 id="all-years">All years, {{ p.label }}</h2>
<p>Every meeting pooled: {{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts, {{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.talks) }} of
them talks. Talk rates are pooled counts (talks ÷ abstracts over all years), compared with the pooled baseline of
{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * p.summary.talk_rate) }}%; the baseline itself ranges from
{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * (years | map(attribute="summary.talk_rate") | min)) }}% to
{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * (years | map(attribute="summary.talk_rate") | max)) }}% by year. Per-year versions of everything
here are on the topic pages.</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="All years">
<a href="#all-phrases">Phrases</a>
{% if "trends_phrases" in trends %}<a href="#phrase-trends">Phrase trends</a>{% endif %}
{% if drivers_json %}<a href="#explorer">Look up a phrase</a>{% endif %}
<a href="#all-institutions">Institutions</a>
<a href="#all-regions">World regions</a>
<a href="#all-metros">Metro areas</a>
<a href="#all-countries">Countries</a>
<a href="#all-authors">Senior authors</a>
<a href="#by-year">By year</a>
</nav>
{{ m.toolbar(basis=True, filter="Institution, country or metro…") }}

<h3 id="all-phrases">Phrases that predict a talk</h3>
<p>Odds ratios are combined across years (Mantel–Haenszel, stratified by year), so a phrase that rose or fell
over time isn't credited with each year's different baseline. {{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.truncated) }} abstracts cut off
in a booklet are left out of the phrase counts.</p>
{{ m.figure("img/all_headline.png", "Dot plot of the phrases most over-represented in ASHG %s talks versus posters, with odds ratios and 95%% confidence intervals." % p.label) }}
{% call m.details("Top 30 phrases each way") %}
<div class="cols">
{% for dir, label in [("talk", "More common in talks"), ("poster", "More common in posters")] %}
<div class="scroll"><p class="table-title"><span class="key" style="background: var(--{{ dir }})"></span>{{ label }}</p>
{{ p.premium[dir] }}</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endcall %}

{% if "trends_phrases" in trends %}
<h3 id="phrase-trends">Phrase trends</h3>
{{ m.figure("img/trends_phrases.png", "For selected phrases, the share of talks and of posters mentioning each one, per year.") }}
{% endif %}

{% if drivers_json %}
<section class="explorer">
<h3 id="explorer">Look up a phrase</h3>
<p>The phrases above plus the top 50 each way across all years. See how often talks and posters mention a phrase
each year, then which first-author institutions and metro areas write about it (among those with at least one
talk mentioning it; an abstract counts for each of its institutions). Hover or focus a row for that institution's
own mention rate.</p>
<div class="filters">
  <label>Find <input type="search" id="drv-search" placeholder="e.g. enhancer" autocomplete="off"></label>
  <label>Phrase <select id="drv-phrase"></select></label>
</div>
<div class="drv-trend">
  <svg id="drv-chart" role="img" viewBox="0 0 360 150"></svg>
  <div><p id="drv-or"></p>
  <div class="legend"><span><i style="background: var(--talk)"></i>share of talks</span><span><i style="background: var(--poster)"></i>share of posters</span></div></div>
</div>
<div class="filters"><span class="lbl">Who writes about it</span><span class="seg" id="drv-year" role="group" aria-label="Year"></span></div>
<p id="drv-summary"></p>
<div class="legend"><span><i style="background: var(--talk)"></i>talks</span><span><i style="background: var(--poster)"></i>posters</span></div>
<div class="cols bars">
  <div><h4>Institutions</h4><div id="drv-institutes"></div></div>
  <div><h4>Metro areas</h4><div id="drv-metros"></div></div>
</div>
<div class="tip" id="drv-tip" role="tooltip" hidden></div>
<script type="application/json" id="drv-data">{{ drivers_json }}</script>
</section>
{% endif %}

<h3 id="all-institutions">Institutions with the highest talk rate</h3>
<p>The 20 highest talk rates among the 50 institutions with the most abstracts over all years. Credit goes to every
institution of the first author, or, with the toggle, of the senior (last) author.</p>
{{ m.basis_figures("all", "institutions", "the 20 institutions with the highest talk rate among the 50 largest", p.label) }}
{% call m.details("All 50 institutions") %}{{ m.by_basis(p.institutions) }}{% endcall %}

<h3 id="all-regions">World regions</h3>
<p>Country of the author's affiliations, grouped into UN regions; an abstract counts once per region.
{% for y in years if y.summary.first_country_coverage < 0.95 %}In {{ y.year }} only
{{ "{:.0%}".format(y.summary.first_country_coverage) }} of abstracts could be placed, and the misses lean non-US.
{% endfor %}</p>
{{ m.basis_figures("all", "regions", "each world region", p.label) }}
{% if "trends_regions" in trends %}
{{ m.figure("img/trends_regions.png", "Talk rate per year for each world region, with 95% intervals.", "Year by year, first author.") }}
{% endif %}
{% call m.details("Regions table") %}{{ m.by_basis(p.regions) }}{% endcall %}

<h3 id="all-metros">Metro areas</h3>
<p>Institutions grouped by metro area; an abstract counts once per metro. Multi-metro institutions are left out
({{ "{:.0%}".format(p.summary.first_metro_coverage) }} of abstracts have a first-author metro). The figure shows the
20 metro areas with the most accepted abstracts over all years. Each meeting's host city tends to bring extra
posters that year.</p>
{{ m.basis_figures("all", "metros", "the 20 metro areas with the most accepted abstracts", p.label) }}
{% if "trends_metros" in trends %}
{{ m.figure("img/trends_metros.png", "Abstracts and talk rate per year for the largest metro areas, with each year's host city marked.", "Year by year, first author.") }}
{% endif %}
{% call m.details("Top 30 metro areas") %}{{ m.by_basis(p.metros) }}{% endcall %}

<h3 id="all-countries">Countries</h3>
<p>The 25 countries with the most abstracts over all years.</p>
{% call m.details("Top 25 countries") %}{{ m.by_basis(p.countries) }}{% endcall %}

<h3 id="all-authors">Senior authors with the highest talk rate</h3>
<p>Senior (last) authors with at least {{ p.min_abstracts }} abstracts over all years, ranked by the lower end of the
95% Wilson interval. The 2022–2024 booklets give only initials, so across years the same person is the same first
initial + last name; for common surnames they must also share an institution, and two different spelled-out first
names (2025) are kept apart.</p>
{{ m.figure("img/all_senior_authors.png", "Talk rate with 95%% intervals for the top senior authors at ASHG %s." % p.label) }}
<div class="scroll">{{ p.senior_authors }}</div>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="by-year">By year</h2>
<div class="cards">
  <a class="card" href="phrases.html">
    <img src="img/{{ latest.year }}_headline.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Phrases</h3>
    <p>In {{ latest.year }}, talks over-index on “{{ latest.top_phrases.talk | join("”, “") }}”; posters on
    “{{ latest.top_phrases.poster | join("”, “") }}”.</p><span class="more">Phrases that predict a talk →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="institutions.html">
    <img src="img/{{ latest.year }}_institutions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Institutions</h3>
    <p>Which of the largest institutions have the highest talk rate, crediting the first or the senior author. Search for your own.</p>
    <span class="more">Institutions →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="geography.html">
    <img src="img/{{ latest.year }}_regions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Geography</h3>
    <p>Talk rate by world region, country and metro area, including the host-city effect.</p>
    <span class="more">Regions, countries and metros →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="authors.html">
    <img src="img/{{ latest.year }}_senior_authors.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Senior authors</h3>
    <p>Senior authors with the most consistent record of talks, ranked by the lower end of a 95% interval.</p>
    <span class="more">Senior authors →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card text-only" href="methods.html">
    <div class="body"><h3>Methods and caveats</h3>
    <p>How the booklets are parsed, how institutions and places are resolved, how phrases are scored, and what
    the numbers can't tell you.</p><span class="more">Methods →</span></div>
  </a>
</div>
{% endblock %}
